WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.170 --> 00:00:03.270
- [Narrator] This is Comac C919.

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.430
China's first homegrown narrow body jet

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.770
that's been in the works
for more than a decade.

00:00:07.770 --> 00:00:11.880
This is a 737 MAX 8, Boeing's
popular narrow body plane

00:00:11.880 --> 00:00:13.563
among airlines worldwide.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:16.920
This type of plane can
cover lots of domestic

00:00:16.920 --> 00:00:18.480
and intercontinental routes.

00:00:18.480 --> 00:00:20.250
Accounting for more
than half of the global

00:00:20.250 --> 00:00:21.873
passenger aircraft fleet.

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.740
And that's a big reason why
Beijing hopes its own model

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:27.720
can compete with western
giants like Boeing

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:29.790
and become the main carrier at home.

00:00:29.790 --> 00:00:33.210
Eventually, one day, taking
on the global airspace.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.120
So we compare the design and
technology of both planes,

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.850
to see how China's deep
reliance on Western parts

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:42.123
could stymie Beijing's ambition
to challenge its US rival.

00:00:43.950 --> 00:00:45.990
Boeing has more than a
hundred years of experience

00:00:45.990 --> 00:00:47.640
with commercial aviation.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:50.310
China in comparison started
exploring the industry

00:00:50.310 --> 00:00:52.890
in the 1970s, but for several decades,

00:00:52.890 --> 00:00:55.380
wasn't able to develop its own airliner.

00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.667
So Boeing became one of
China's go-to companies.

00:00:57.667 --> 00:01:00.690
- In China, Boeing has had
a great couple decades.

00:01:00.690 --> 00:01:02.640
- [Narrator] Richard
Aboulafia is managing director

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:04.230
with aerodynamic advisory

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:07.590
and aerospace and defense
consultancy based in Michigan.

00:01:07.590 --> 00:01:08.670
For more than 30 years,

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:10.740
he's been tracking global aviation markets

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:13.110
with Boeing as one of his main focuses.

00:01:13.110 --> 00:01:16.530
- If you look back at
China economic growth

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.330
and air travel demand growth,

00:01:18.330 --> 00:01:20.490
it really took off in the '90s.

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:23.670
And sometime in the 2000s,
that began to translate

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:26.190
into very large jetliner sales numbers.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:27.450
- [Narrator] Boeing jetliner sales

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.640
hit a record high in 2017.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.000
The American giant sent more
than 200 planes to China.

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:35.940
That's about a quarter of
all its deliveries that year.

00:01:35.940 --> 00:01:39.720
It also has a 737 completion
and delivery plant there.

00:01:39.720 --> 00:01:42.360
Today, about 40% of
China's passenger fleet

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:44.280
comes from Boeing, with more than half

00:01:44.280 --> 00:01:46.980
of the planes held by
the European giant Airbus

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.560
which also has an assembly plan in China.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:51.240
So in order to reduce its reliance

00:01:51.240 --> 00:01:53.070
on the two Western jet liners,

00:01:53.070 --> 00:01:55.740
the Chinese government
has been focused on Comac,

00:01:55.740 --> 00:01:57.810
which was established in 2008.

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:00.270
And Chinese President Xi
Jinping has especially

00:02:00.270 --> 00:02:02.912
been keen on creating a domestic airliner.

00:02:02.912 --> 00:02:05.912
(speaking Mandarin)

00:02:14.370 --> 00:02:15.480
- [Narrator] China hasn't revealed

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:17.310
how much it's invested in Comac

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:19.260
but some aerospace analysts estimate

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:21.390
that the state owned company
has received somewhere

00:02:21.390 --> 00:02:25.290
between 49 and $72
billion in government aid.

00:02:25.290 --> 00:02:28.860
- That was and is a
national goal for China

00:02:28.860 --> 00:02:32.280
to be able to compete
against the US and Boeing.

00:02:32.280 --> 00:02:33.960
- [Narrator] Alex Krutz
is managing director

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.060
with US-based aerospace consulting firm,

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:37.890
Patriot Industrial Partners,

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.840
and he's been following Comax programs

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.460
for about seven years.

00:02:41.460 --> 00:02:43.950
- [Alex] Ultimately,
designing and building

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:47.100
a successful commercial
airliners is very technologically

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.740
advanced for countries to be able to do.

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:52.290
- [Narrator] So to develop a
successful commercial airliner,

00:02:52.290 --> 00:02:55.140
China has been eyeing
western designs like Boeing.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:58.350
The two jets are both narrow
bodies with a single aisle.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:00.180
They're also about the same size

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:02.583
and carry a similar number of passengers.

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.150
Even the engines aren't too different.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:08.550
- They're from CFM,
which is a joint venture

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:11.610
between General Electric
and Safran of France,

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:13.650
and they're very similar engines

00:03:13.650 --> 00:03:16.770
with roughly similar levels of technology.

00:03:16.770 --> 00:03:17.970
- [Narrator] Both engines are models

00:03:17.970 --> 00:03:20.430
from the LEAP one series from CFM.

00:03:20.430 --> 00:03:23.940
- [Richard] LEAP-1B is for
Boeing, LEAP-1C is for Comac.

00:03:23.940 --> 00:03:26.220
- [Narrator] But the MAX
8 and the C919 need more

00:03:26.220 --> 00:03:27.900
than just the engines to take off.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:32.160
- They need other systems
like the mechanical systems,

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:34.980
landing gears or management systems

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:37.500
avionics for the cockpits.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.150
- [Narrator] These components
and their supply chains

00:03:39.150 --> 00:03:41.310
have played a big role
in establishing Boeing

00:03:41.310 --> 00:03:43.650
as an industry leader over the years.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:46.020
With decades of experience,
the American company

00:03:46.020 --> 00:03:47.730
has developed steady relationships

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:50.490
with its partners and
suppliers at home and abroad,

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:53.040
and most of them are
close allies of the US.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.660
- It's very much an
international creation.

00:03:54.660 --> 00:03:58.290
Boeing's major international
partner is Japan, Britain,

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:01.890
France, Canada, Italy,
Germany, and many others.

00:04:01.890 --> 00:04:03.240
- [Narrator] Those
partnerships have helped Boeing

00:04:03.240 --> 00:04:05.340
secure some of the most
advanced technologies

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:07.350
for its aircraft like the cockpit,

00:04:07.350 --> 00:04:09.240
which is the brain of the plane.

00:04:09.240 --> 00:04:11.160
Comac also needs a global supply chain

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:12.930
to put the C919 together,

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:15.750
especially from American
and European companies.

00:04:15.750 --> 00:04:18.150
But aerospace analysts
say some foreign suppliers

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.910
have been reluctant to provide
state-of-the-art components

00:04:20.910 --> 00:04:23.523
over concerns about their
intellectual property.

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:27.060
This has saddled the C919
with older technology

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:31.110
than the 737 MAX 8 and
even the Airbus 320neo.

00:04:31.110 --> 00:04:34.050
But this may not be the biggest
risk to the Comac project.

00:04:34.050 --> 00:04:37.523
- There's this, I guess,
sword hanging over the 919,

00:04:37.523 --> 00:04:39.900
and a lot of it does
come down to geopolitics.

00:04:39.900 --> 00:04:41.370
- [Narrator] The US has long accused China

00:04:41.370 --> 00:04:43.380
as seeking to steal advanced technologies

00:04:43.380 --> 00:04:46.830
for use in its military, which
Beijing repeatedly denied.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:50.100
In January last year, the Trump
administration added Comac

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:52.470
to a list of companies
that it said supported

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:55.860
China's military, curbing the
plane manufacturer's access

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:58.110
to American technology and funding.

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:59.340
Comac was later removed

00:04:59.340 --> 00:05:01.950
when President Biden issued a new list.

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:03.480
The Chinese company didn't respond

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.490
to a request for comment
about the blacklist

00:05:05.490 --> 00:05:07.680
and concerns over IP infringement,

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.690
as well as whether geopolitical tensions

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:12.363
could pose a risk to its C919 program.

00:05:14.460 --> 00:05:15.810
Even if these vulnerabilities

00:05:15.810 --> 00:05:18.180
with sourcing critical
western parts disappeared,

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:21.540
aviation experts say Comax
still has other challenges.

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:23.340
- Learning how to build it, conforming,

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.920
that is to say each
article is exactly the same

00:05:25.920 --> 00:05:29.340
as the previous one,
that's a major challenge.

00:05:29.340 --> 00:05:31.680
That's one of the easiest
places to stumble.

00:05:31.680 --> 00:05:32.940
- [Narrator] And another stumbling block

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:34.710
if and when China goes global,

00:05:34.710 --> 00:05:36.630
the lack of a worldwide support system

00:05:36.630 --> 00:05:39.660
for operators to obtain C919 spare parts

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:41.520
or receive maintenance and repairs.

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:44.280
- Got a service at aftermarket
support for the airplanes.

00:05:44.280 --> 00:05:47.160
So there's vast networks that Boeing has

00:05:47.160 --> 00:05:48.813
that Comac has to develop.

00:05:49.740 --> 00:05:51.120
- [Narrator] For Boeing, the US giant

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:55.020
also has its own problems,
especially in the Chinese market.

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:57.060
As trade tensions broke out between the US

00:05:57.060 --> 00:06:00.660
and China in 2017, Beijing
froze nearly all orders

00:06:00.660 --> 00:06:02.820
and deliveries of Boeing's planes.

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:04.230
Since early 2019,

00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:07.320
the country has also kept
the 737 MAX grounded,

00:06:07.320 --> 00:06:11.520
after two fatal crashes
in Indonesia and Ethiopia.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:14.280
Boeing says it continues to
work with global regulators

00:06:14.280 --> 00:06:17.310
and customers to safely return the 737 MAX

00:06:17.310 --> 00:06:19.290
and cease China as an important market

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:21.060
for the company's commercial planes,

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:23.853
urging dialogue between
Beijing and Washington.

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:28.170
Despite the challenges,
Comac is moving forward.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:30.450
The C919 marked a major milestone

00:06:30.450 --> 00:06:32.910
in September towards carrying passengers,

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:34.500
and the company has plans to develop

00:06:34.500 --> 00:06:36.570
a wide body plane as well.

00:06:36.570 --> 00:06:38.100
But for Comac to rival Boeing,

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.653
it'll be a long and
perhaps bumpy flight ahead.

